  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to a Class Sui Generis (HMO - house in multiple occupation) and 2-storey side extension, part single part 2-storey rear extension, rear dormer involving rooflights to front, with associated amenity, cycle and refuse storage.\r",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The site lies within areas at risk of surface water and fluvial flooding in a 1 in 100 year event (+17% climate change allowance). The submitted Flood Risk Assessment fails to demonstrate that the development would be safe for its lifetime or would not increase flood risk elsewhere, as it does not provide finished floor levels (including the required freeboard to ensure safety for any ground-floor sleeping accommodation), demonstrate that on site flood storage would not be reduced (or provide level-for-level compensation), or include a Flood Management/Evacuation Plan demonstrating a Very Low Hazard evacuation route (FD2320). The proposal is therefore contrary to guidance in Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024); Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021); Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD59, DMD60 and DMD61 of the Development Management Document (2014).\r",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the inadequate and limited size of the rooflight serving Bedroom 9, would fail to provide satisfactory levels of daylight and outlook to that room. As a result, Bedroom 9 would constitute substandard and inappropriate accommodation that would not meet the reasonable needs of future occupiers, contrary to Sections 2 and 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D5 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD5, DMD6, DMD8 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
